index 4479b53..629dce4 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,43 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP browser tools
+
+WebMCP is a progressive enhancement for supporting browsers in a secure context.
+It uses the browser's `document.modelContext` API through `use-webmcp-tool`;
+unsupported browsers retain the standard search and reading-list UI. See the
+[Chrome WebMCP documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp).
+
+The header registers `open_search` and `open_reading_list` on every page. These
+open the visible flyouts, making their declarative form tools discoverable:
+
+- `search_articles`: accepts `query`, searches article titles and summaries, and
+  returns matching articles with their slugs and links.
+- `manage_reading_list`: accepts `action` (`view`, `add`, or `remove`) and an
+  article `slug` for add/remove. Results contain the updated session reading list.
+  Add/remove are idempotent; existing bookmark buttons retain toggle behavior.
+
+Both forms support normal submission and agent invocation. Agent submissions use
+`SubmitEvent.respondWith()` to return results after updating the UI, without
+navigating away. Form values are read from `FormData`, including values populated
+by the browser agent. Closing a flyout removes its form tool.
+
+The client also registers these imperative tools:
+
+| Tool | Available on | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `list_articles` | Every page | Article metadata, slugs, and links |
+| `get_current_article` | Article pages | Current title, summary, body text, and link |
+| `get_coffee_brew` | `coffee-alchemy` | Coffee utility response |
+| `get_tide_levels` | `coastal-pulse` | Tide utility response, including redirect metadata |
+| `get_plant_stats` | `silent-architects` | Plant statistics response |
+| `get_article_popularity` | `super-bowl-lx` | Popularity response for the required `id` article slug |
+
+Article API utilities preserve the site's intentional DevTools failure scenarios;
+HTTP failures return status and response data rather than reporting success.
+Imperative network tools forward execution cancellation signals, and React hook
+cleanup removes tools when components unmount during Astro navigation.
+
+Validation: `pnpm run build` compiles the client and server bundles without
+starting a server. A build does not verify browser tool discovery or invocation.
